Backport JDK-8308780: Fix the Java Integer types on Windows

11 spells the windows JNI types as MSVC extensions, "long" and "__int64". 17
moved them to "int" and "long long" and every release since kept that. With jint
as long, a jint argument on win64 is neither int32_t (int) nor intptr_t (long
long), so it sits exactly between the two movptr overloads that exist, as
macroAssembler_x86.hpp puts it, "so that int32_t and intptr_t are not the same
and we have ambiguous declarations":

  c1_LIRAssembler_x86.cpp:617: error: call to member function 'movptr' is ambiguous

Both types keep their width on windows, so this is the same ABI, which is what
let upstream make the change at all.

The other nine files are the companions upstream changed in the same commit,
without which the tree no longer builds once jint is int: AwtMenu::GetItem is
declared long in the header and defined jint in the .cpp, the AWT icon and arc
code hands long arrays to jint APIs, and c1_Canonicalizer's extra overload
exists only to convert int to a jint that used to be long.

Adapted where 11 differs from 17: ShellFolder2 still uses stack arrays rather
than safe_Malloc, and GDIRenderer has two arc sites rather than one.

Upstream: https://bugs.openjdk.org/browse/JDK-8308780

